From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa2-lite: synchronize mapped TX buffers before BAM

The AP BAM producer reads packet buffers through the IPA SMMU stream.  Make
the DMA ownership transition explicit after mapping the skb and before
publishing its descriptor to BAM.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
--- a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
@@ -3008,6 +3008,12 @@ static int ipa_enqueue_skb(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *ndev, struct ipa_ep *ep)
 	if (dma_mapping_error(dev, addr))
 		goto free_skb;
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep the payload visible to the AP BAM producer before its descriptor
+	 * is published through the event register.
+	 */
+	dma_sync_single_for_device(dev, addr, len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+
 	desc.addr = addr;
 	desc.size = len;
 	desc.flags = ep->is_rx ? DESC_FLAG_INT : DESC_FLAG_EOT;
